  5.3 Policy Making for Italy’s Higher Education System
              号




        Based on the previous analysis, we propose a series of policies to achieve the ideal health
  state of the higher education system.
        Policy 1: Increase government spending on education, especially on post-secondary
             信




  education. In Italy, all public universities are almost free of tuition. Only after 2000, the Italian
  Ministry of Education began to impose symbolic fees on public institutions due to the influx
    微




  of foreign students.[13] So the development of higher education is largely dependent on govern-
  ment support.
        Policy 2: Create an open and inclusive academic environment to improve interna-




